{"text": "JOSEPH T. DETERS\n\nHAMILTON COUNTY PROSECUTING ATTORNEY\n\u2018ADMINISTRATION OWISION\n230 EAST NINTH STREET, SUITE 4000\n\u2018CINCINNATL OM 45022151,\nPHONE: (51) 246-3000,\nFAX ($1) 846-3017\nWww HGPROS ORG\nWRITER'S DRECT DAL NUMBER\n(619) 0\u00a26 3008\n\nMay 17, 2019\n\nCouncilmember David Mann\nCity Council, City of Cincinnati\n\nSuite 349, City Hall\n801 Plum Street\nCincinnati, OH 45202\n\nDear Councilmember Mann:\n\nIhave read with great interest the proposal to decriminalize marijuana under the\n100 or 200 gram levels.\n\nAs you probably know, | have supported the decriminalization of small amounts of\nHowever, | feel these levels of weight are too high in terms of\npersonal use. It may affect our presumption of Unlawful Possession and Trafficking in\n\nmarijuana in the past.\n\nDrugs.\n\nI would urge council to meet with police and prosecutors to determine a minimal\namount to decriminalize.\n\nJTD/mag\n\nRespectfully,\n\nCnn Dt\n\nJoseph T. Deters\n\nProsecuting Attorney",
